     "documents": [
      {
       "type": "Progress Notes",
       "title": "Same-Day Visit",
       "author": "PCP",
       "date": "2023-03-17T13:40",
       "body": "Texted this morning: two days of nausea and vomiting, not eating much, and she is seeing halos around the lights. Seen same day.\n\n70-year-old with paroxysmal AF and HFrEF on digoxin 0.125 mg daily, warfarin, furosemide 40, metoprolol, benztropine. Amiodarone stopped in 2021 (lung toxicity, then thyrotoxicosis). No new medicines. No diarrhea, no abdominal pain, no fever. Keeping fluids down in sips.\nAllergies: sulfa drugs (rash).\n\nExam: BP 130/80, HR 60, RR 16. Looks tired but not toxic. Mucous membranes slightly dry. Heart regular. Lungs clear. Abdomen soft, nontender. Mild pedal edema on both sides. Otherwise unremarkable.\n\nOffice ECG: sinus rhythm with occasional PVCs.\nStat labs (back 1:15 pm): digoxin 2.5 ng/mL, potassium 4.5, creatinine 1.2, INR 2.3.\n\nA/P: Digoxin toxicity: GI symptoms and visual halos with a level of 2.5; creatinine 1.2 likely reduced clearance. Hemodynamically fine, no high-grade block or dangerous arrhythmia, potassium normal, so no antidote needed. Hold digoxin. Repeat digoxin level and BMP Tuesday. Called her cardiologist's office with the results. Strict ED precautions for fainting, slow or racing pulse, or worsening vomiting; she has my cell."
      }
     ]
